        "path": "_m/s/t/q/4/al-rifa-i-mosque-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Mausoleum of Sheikh Ali al-Rifa'i.JPG",
        "caption": "Mausoleum of Sheikh Ali Abu Shibbak al-Rifa'i, located in the Rifa'i Mosque in Cairo, Egypt. Sheikh Ali Abu Shibbak was a medieval Sufi Muslim \"saint\", and the grandson of the founder of the Rifa'i order, Sheikh Ahmad al-Rifa'i (1106–1182). The site of the current mosque was originally occupied by a zawya containing the tombs of Sheikh Ali Abu Shibbak and other sheikhs. The zawya was demolished and replaced by the current mosque in the 19th century by order of Khushiyar Kadin, the mother of Khedive Isma'il Pasha of Egypt.",
